                                "sense_id": "91b74fa0-94ce-3140-82bf-72cbb29961dd",
                                "text": "Reports were common of a Sino-British agreement for British co-operation in the economic development of South China, including British financing of a railway in Hainan, the establishment of an airdrome on Tungsha Island southeast of Hongkong, an oil depot in the Sesha Islands southwest of Hainan, and the development of mines in South China."
